Reeses Pieces:

    Since they are a peaceful blend of two
    incompatible substances, they have the quality
    that they will turn a monster peaceful (not
    tame) if tossed to that monster.

    Normally highly nutritious and calming, can
    clear a "cause fear".

    However, if eaten while flying, in any of the
    senses of levitating, riding a flying steed,
    flying oneself (presumably polymorphed) or
    hallucinating, there is a small chance of
    instadeath from anaphylactic shock.

M&Ms:

    If eaten, their intrinsic: "prevents fingers
    from being sticky" will allow the adventurer to
    drop one hand-held cursed object (including
    shields) on the next turn only.

    If _worn_, and "enchant armor" read, will become
    _either_:

    an "armor of thin candy shell", worn like a
    cloak, providing no AC improvement unless
    further enchanted, but making the PC very
    attractive to nurses;

    _or_

    a technicolor dreamcoat, also worn like a
    cloak, which causes restful sleep like the
    amulet, and is likely to be cursed,

    _or_

    a coat of many colors, which aggravates monsters
    of the PC's own species, but adds 2 to charisma.
    [Unless one is a tourist, when it subtracts 2
    from charisma, has the same affect in shops as a
    Hawaiian shirt, and is cursed].

    These three cannot be distinguished until the
    enchanted armor is re-identified.

Mounds Bars:

    If included in a stack of stuff being polypiled,
    reduces by 90% the chance of golems being
    generated or stuff vanishing.

Rollos:

